      "id": "S13",
      "sourceSha256": "f17a81d0bdd38dbaa80667b5ed5a39eaecf7f5c1953d5b2925363710bab03fc9",
      "observation": "Viewed all 120 candidate frames, four complete scene sheets, temporal overview, the one printed-face detector crop and all 120 tracked print crops, and compared the original S13 scene and M01 design. The earlier clear open-eye interval is slowed twofold. Both violet-pink irises, round gold glasses and face proportions remain recognizable and stable; the late narrowing in the rejected complete original is excluded. The same head-out adult female holds the umbrella; her own other hand enters below the charm near the end, without an added person. Ordinary wet empty street, feminine white/violet/gold costume, no real face or reflection, no cut. Native small print remains soft; this is not a pixel-identical restoration. Original raw and rejected review are preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "S17",
      "sourceSha256": "75fcbf85738af14e68d128cd3877a032c82c6fa16818e454bc606983ef86ee97",
      "observation": "This exact selected file was independently generated under the separately reviewed image-only S17 plan cb08b9e8c02e2df4512d5669aeaa285323f33ed1d9628df41451ca961f7861bd, then imported with its own actual raw parent, job and request provenance. It supersedes the rejected R2 closed-eye source and earlier retimes. All 120 full source frames, both printed-face candidates, temporal sheet, native contexts 0/119 and all 120 tracked print crops were viewed and directly compared with original scene and master artwork. Open violet-pink eyes, round gold glasses, eyelid shapes and facial layout remain recognizable and fixed at native detail, without closing, iris drift, extra eyes or facial performance. No pixel-identical reconstruction claim. One rigid original stand and base remain on the ordinary greenhouse table in almost stationary framing; subtle background leaves/light move. No real people, face fragments, extra body parts, reflections, extra stand, letters or cut. Original white violet gold printed female costume retained. Full five seconds reviewed, three seconds used in the updated director. The independent generator plan and all rejected originals remain archived."
    },
    {
      "id": "S26",
      "sourceSha256": "e9fbe321cc09ecce3c411090994b946fdb1cf832c431df3ed747087b081a97c7",
      "observation": "Viewed all 120 complete native frames in four sheets, temporal overview, all 13 detector crops, and all 120 tracked face-detail crops, and compared the original S26 scene artwork. Empty car passenger seat with the same lilac pouch; ordinary dry roadside and fence move past the window continuously. No occupant, passerby, real face, reflection or added body part. Pouch seam and zipper cause false face detections. Printed forward-facing violet eyes, round gold glasses and face proportions stay open, coherent and fixed on the fabric; no blink or expression change. Native print is small and soft rather than pixel-identical to the reference. No internal cut or impossible background event."
    }
